# ---- 1.1 (3.71) · feel, rows, motion, perform
config (FEEL, all neutral by default — 1.0 songs play the same notes): humanize 0…1 (±12 ms, ±25 % velocity, seeded) · accent 0…1
(beats ×1+0.45a, off-beat 16ths ×1−0.35a) · rolls 0…1 (hat / open hat / perc / shaker: chance rolls×0.5 of 2–4 hits in the step) ·
fill off|2|4|8|16 (the half-bar before every N bars: snare, ghost, perc at least 0.55 density, energy +0.35) · evolve off|1|2|4|8
(seed + 101 every N bars) · loop 1 bar|2 bars · rows {mute, solo, level 0…1.5, chance −1…1 (× the hit chance), pad 0…15}.
ui hook row_set {row, mute?, solo?, level?, chance?, pad?}. perform: true → m1…m4, _motion, _perform (core/motion.js).
window: Play · Feel · Motion · Perform tabs.

# ---- ADDENDUM 2026-11-06 · 3.132 the boom bap style (everything above kept verbatim — Axiom 9)
# his words: "i also want to be able to make lofi" (2026-11-05) · "yes" (2026-11-06, to the Lofi setup: specs/eravos.lofi-setup.spec)
style_boom_bap:
  - a sixth style "boom bap" (lofi, hip-hop): kick on 1 and the "and" of 2, the second bar pushing (steps 0, 6, 10 · 16, 22, 26, 27),
    snare on 2 and 4, eighth-note hats (softer off the beat), ghost snares before the backbeats, an open hat at the end of bar 2
  - default unchanged (dubstep); the five styles' maps unchanged (styleMap returns the same for them)
  - the lofi feel comes from the settings, as packs: Swing ~0.5, Humanize, low ENERGY (packs/lofi)
proof: groove-gen tests — boom bap's kick and snare where they should be; the five styles unchanged

